Define j_* = N-|Y_0|-m^* after plateau terminalization.
Then exactly

  s=Delta_Lambda-d_int
   =|C^partial|-|O|+j_*,

and

  zeta-s = h(G)-j_*.

For a basis-closed tube shield W, let O_iso be surviving O rows with no surviving neighbor and let

  Q=sum_i max(0, |O_i|-|C_i|).

The Section-174 three-sector condition is exactly equivalent to

  Q >= j_* + |W\O| - |O_iso|.

So the missing theorem is specifically an exterior-sink-surplus theorem, not a generic Schur-rank theorem.
```
